---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About — CopperTrace">
  <article class="article">
    <div class="article-meta">About</div>
    <h1>CopperTrace</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      An independent engineering notebook documenting practical work in electronics,
      embedded systems, RF, test and measurement, automation and hardware reverse engineering.
    </p>

    <h2>About me</h2>
    <p>
      I am a Chief Electronics Engineer within Radiotherapy Physics, leading a specialist
      engineering team responsible for the maintenance, repair and technical support of complex
      equipment used in cancer treatment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Although I now have a leadership role, I have always enjoyed the practical side of
      engineering: fault finding, understanding how systems work, building test equipment and
      turning ideas into working hardware and software.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside of work I spend much of my engineering time experimenting with embedded systems,
      microcontrollers, RF and SDR, Linux, test equipment and hardware reverse engineering.
      I enjoy projects that cross the boundary between electronics and software, particularly
      when measurement and automation can make a difficult problem easier to understand.
    </p>

    <h2>Why CopperTrace?</h2>
    <p>
      CopperTrace is where I document selected personal engineering projects and the process
      behind them. The aim is to keep a useful record of measurements, experiments, failures
      and solutions rather than only showing the finished result.
    </p>
    <p>
      Current work includes reverse engineering compact laboratory power hardware, automated
      electronic test infrastructure and modular RF sensing research.
    </p>

    <h2>Areas of interest</h2>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag">Electronics</span>
      <span class="tag">Embedded systems</span>
      <span class="tag">Test &amp; measurement</span>
      <span class="tag">RF / SDR</span>
      <span class="tag">Linux</span>
      <span class="tag">Automation</span>
      <span class="tag">Reverse engineering</span>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      CopperTrace documents independent personal projects. It is not affiliated with my employer
      and does not contain patient, clinical or non-public workplace information.
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
